# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FX Desk — environment variables. Never commit real values.
# On Vercel, set these in Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# There are TWO deployments of this one repository, and the difference between
# them is this file. Give both halves' variables to one project and the desk's
# own application is holding a credential that can open companies.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === THE DESK =============================================================
# Supabase TRANSACTION pooler (port 6543), role ex_app_login.
# Supabase Dashboard → Connect → "Transaction pooler", then:
#   postgresql://ex_app_login.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# It must NOT be `postgres`. That role has BYPASSRLS, which switches off every
# row-level-security guard in the product — one company could read another's books.
DATABASE_URL=
# Connections per server instance (default 5). Keep instances × this below the pooler's pool size.
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=5
# Seconds to wait for a connection to open (default 30). Opening one through Supabase's pooler
# from India measures 0.4–6 s and varies; the old 10 s ceiling produced CONNECT_TIMEOUT at
# sign-in. Raise it further on a slow line rather than lowering it.
# DATABASE_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=30

# === THE SUPER ADMIN CONSOLE (/platform) ==================================
# Role ex_platform_login, created once at go-live:
#   CREATE ROLE ex_platform_login LOGIN PASSWORD '<from the password manager>' IN ROLE ex_platform;
#   GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA ex TO ex_platform_login;
#
# It is not a member of ex_app. It has no privilege on a single table and can only
# execute the ex.fn_platform_* functions, none of which returns money.
#
# LEAVE THIS BLANK ON THE DESK'S OWN DEPLOYMENT. Without it /platform does not work
# at all, which is the intended state there. Set it only on the console's project.
# On one developer machine running both halves it is normal to set both.
DATABASE_PLATFORM_URL=
# DATABASE_PLATFORM_POOL_MAX=2

# === SHARED ===============================================================
# Upstash Redis (region ap-south-1 / Mumbai) → REST API credentials
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

SESSION_COOKIE_NAME=fx_sid
PLATFORM_COOKIE_NAME=fx_psid
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Development only: 1 = open the portal shell without login (ignored in production)
FX_PREVIEW=0

# Admin connection (session pooler, port 5432, role postgres).
# For `npm run test:db` and scripts/create-super-admin.mjs ONLY. NEVER set on Vercel.
# DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing else is read. In particular there is no DIRECT_URL, DB_SCHEMA,
# DATABASE_MAX_CONNECTIONS, DATABASE_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS, DATABASE_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS
# or REDIS_*_TTL — every query is schema-qualified and the timeouts and TTLs are
# set in code (src/lib/db.ts, src/lib/redis.ts). Adding them here does nothing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
